# The line-coverage floor, in percent. THE one place it is stated.
#
# `scripts/coverage.sh` reads this number and fails when the suite's measured
# line coverage falls below it; CI runs that script (see
# .github/workflows/codacy-coverage.yml). Raising it is a one-line diff and is
# the intended way to ratchet — lower it only with a reason in the commit
# message.
#
# Deliberately about a point and a half under the number actually achieved
# (89.70 % at the time of writing). A floor set at the exact measurement goes red
# on the first honest refactor that adds a guard clause nobody has a test for,
# and a gate that is red the week it lands is a gate everybody learns to skip.
#
# docs/coverage.md carries the real number, what moved it, and the list of what
# genuinely cannot be covered from a headless suite.
88.0
